cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AutoBee
message: >-
  If you use this software, or report results obtained from it, please cite the
  report below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Oloruntoba
    given-names: Daniel Olamide
    affiliation: Bingham University
repository-code: "https://github.com/Daniel-16/autobee"
abstract: >-
  AutoBee is an autonomous aerial surveillance system that lets a non-pilot
  issue a natural-language command and have a low-cost drone plan a survey, fly
  it under closed-loop velocity control, avoid obstacles from its camera, count
  crowds, and report back. A language-model planner sits outside the inner
  control loop behind an explicit validation gate; the simulator (Gazebo) and a
  real DJI Tello share an identical ROS 2 topic graph, so the same autonomy code
  runs on both.
keywords:
  - autonomous drone
  - aerial surveillance
  - ROS 2
  - large language model
  - mission planning
  - obstacle avoidance
  - crowd analytics
  - DJI Tello
license-url: "https://github.com/Daniel-16/autobee/blob/main/LICENSE"
